# doc/codex/issues/0072 criterion 5, the '-r' row.  The deck is that issue's
# six-byte reproducer verbatim -- a title line and an .op dot card, no comment
# block, because the deck IS the reproducer; the commentary lives here, in the
# .invoke and .files siblings and in Makefile.am.
#
# Zero, and it is the right answer rather than a bug.  Every other op-empty-*
# deck in this directory exits 1, because a nodeless .op run builds an empty
# plot and the guard at src/frontend/dotcards.c:225 reports it.  Under -r that
# plot is never built: OUTpBeginPlot() takes its writeOut arm and calls
# fileInit() instead of plotInit() (src/frontend/outitf.c:494-:497), so
# plot_list gains nothing.  ft_cktcoms() still runs -- from the OTHER of its
# two call sites, main.c:1573, the rflag arm of the batch epilogue, with
# terse=TRUE, where every other op-empty-* deck arrives at main.c:1581 with
# terse=FALSE -- but its setcplot("op") answers NULL, so the body holding the
# guard is never entered.  The run streams a rawfile and exits normally.
#
# So this is not "the same mistake, forgiven on one route".  It is a different
# path through the simulator that never had the defect, and criterion 5's
# requirement for it is the opposite of criterion 1's: the row has to be shown
# NOT to have moved, and the file it writes has to be a valid raw file or no
# file at all -- not a third thing.  op-empty-raw.files asserts the file and
# two of its header lines; that the row does not move under the fix was
# measured by reverting the guard and re-running this deck, in this batch's
# receipt 03.
0
